{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked me to build the Cinescope cinema seat-booking web app described in spec/README.md, as the Angular 22 application `cinescope` (apps/cinescope) in the Nx/pnpm workspace at /workspace/project, following spec/stack.md. Work is split into tickets 01–07 in spec/tickets/, to be implemented in order. Constraints: no questions to the user, choose the simplest option where the spec is silent, and finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. Standing rules from the spec: use pnpm only; app on port 4200; do not add dependencies; do not edit db.json; desktop only (1280×720+); English only; use Angular Material components for buttons, text fields, checkboxes, toasts and datepicker; `data-testid` and data attributes exactly as in spec section 9; do not build section 11 out-of-scope items; do not change date logic. No commits or PRs were requested.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Angular 22 standalone components, zoneless (default), signals (`signal`, `computed`), `inject()`, control flow (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`).\n   - Angular Router: routes with `canActivate` functional guards (`CanActivateFn`, `createUrlTree`), `ActivatedRoute.paramMap` / `queryParamMap`, `router.navigate([], {queryParams})`, `navigateByUrl`.\n   - HttpClient (`provideHttpClient()`), RxJS (`forkJoin`, `switchMap`, `catchError`, `EMPTY`, `tap`, `map`), `takeUntilDestroyed` from `@angular/core/rxjs-interop`.\n   - Angular Material 22: MatButtonModule, MatDatepickerModule (with provideNativeDateAdapter), MatFormFieldModule/MatInputModule (matInput), MatCheckboxModule, MatSnackBar (openFromComponent, MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA).\n   - sessionStorage-backed booking (key 'cinescope.booking').\n   - Seat-map geometry in CSS flex: 36px slot per seat (32px + 2px margins), 72px aisle, 144px entrance, 68px couch, 40px row labels; all rows 1088px wide.\n   - Vitest unit tests via `pnpm nx test cinescope` (@angular/build:unit-test, jsdom).\n   - json-server 0.17.4 backend on port 3000 (db.json).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts\n      - Adds provideHttpClient(); providers: provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners, provideRouter(appRoutes), provideHttpClient(), provideNativeDateAdapter().\n   - apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts (final)\n      ```ts\n      export const appRoutes: Routes = [\n        { path: '', component: MovieListComponent },\n        { path: 'screenings/:id/seats', component: SeatSelectionComponent },\n        { path: 'screenings/:id/summary', component: SummaryComponent, canActivate: [unpaidBookingGuard] },\n        { path: 'screenings/:id/checkout', component: CheckoutComponent, canActivate: [unpaidBookingGuard] },\n        { path: 'confirmation', component: ConfirmationComponent, canActivate: [paidBookingGuard] },\n        { path: '**', redirectTo: '' },\n      ];\n      ```\n   - core/models.ts — Movie, Screening, Customer, ReservationRequest, Reservation interfaces per spec 2.1.\n   - core/api.service.ts — ApiService: movies(), screeningsOn(date), screeningWithMovie(id), reserve(request); API_URL 'http://localhost:3000'.\n   - core/dates.ts — startOfToday, addDays, weekdayName, toIsoDate, parseIsoDate (returns Date|null with round-trip check), showDate(isoDate, time).\n   - core/auditorium.ts — SeatState, SeatItem, CouchItem, AisleItem, EntranceItem, LayoutItem, AuditoriumRow, seatId, buildAuditorium(occupied, selected); row 15 uses couches; entrance in rows 1–10; aisles before cols 5 and 21; accessible = row 1 cols 10–15; stateOf priority unavailable > selected > accessible > available.\n   - core/seat-units.ts — MAX_SEATS_PER_BOOKING=10, SeatUnit, parseSeatId, sortSeatIds, toUnits, unitLabel, unitDescription, bookingTotal.\n   - core/pricing.ts — unitPrice (couch 89; rows 1–5 25; 6–10 32; 11–14 39), formatPrice.\n   - core/booking.service.ts — CheckoutForm, Booking, exported emptyCheckoutForm(), BookingService {booking signal, open, setSeats, setForm, markPaid, clear, private patch/save/restore}.\n   - core/booking.guards.ts — unpaidBookingGuard, paidBookingGuard.\n   - core/toast.service.ts and core/toast.component.ts — ToastService.show(msg) (duration 4000); ToastComponent with host data-testid=\"toast\".\n   - movies/movie-list.component.ts/.html/.scss — MovieListComponent (day picker, datepicker, loading/error/empty/loaded states, retry(), selectDay, pickDate, openScreening; cards computed from movies and screenings).\n   - seats/seat-selection.component.ts/.html/.scss — SeatSelectionComponent (load, booking.open, toggle with cap toast, legend, selected-seats panel, Cancel/Continue with goToSummary()).\n   - summary/summary.component.ts/.html/.scss — SummaryComponent (items, remove, back, confirm, total).\n   - checkout/checkout-validation.ts — validateCheckout, hasErrors (rules per spec 7).\n   - checkout/checkout.component.ts/.html/.scss — CheckoutComponent (fields with testids, error elements only while shown, pay flow, Back).\n   - confirmation/confirmation.component.ts/.html/.scss — ConfirmationComponent (heading, message with email, finish() clears booking and navigates to '/').\n   - Specs (all passing): core/auditorium.spec.ts, core/seat-units.spec.ts, checkout/checkout-validation.spec.ts, core/dates.spec.ts.\n   - Deleted: core/route-placeholder.component.ts (no longer referenced).\n   - Not yet edited: spec/tickets/01–07 checkboxes and Status lines; .pnpm-store/ (untracked, appeared during work; probably pnpm's store created by my pnpm invocations — verify before removing).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `pnpm nx build` aborted with ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY (pnpm's verify-deps step tries to purge node_modules non-interactively). Fix: set env `pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run=false` for pnpm nx commands (`./node_modules/.bin/nx` also works). Do not set CI=true (would purge node_modules). This is an environment quirk to mention to the user.\n   - `pnpm api` failed for the same reason. Fix: started json-server directly with `./node_modules/.bin/json-server --watch db.json --port 3000` (running; reachable via [::1]:3000; Node fetch to 127.0.0.1 returned ECONNREFUSED initially).\n   - TS2341 in movie-list template: `load()` was private but used in `(click)`. Fix: added public `retry()` and bound the Retry button to it.\n   - Unit-test failure: in seat-units.spec.ts I called `.reverse()` on toUnits output, which is already sorted by row. Fixed by removing `.reverse()`; all 26 tests now pass.\n   - No user feedback corrections were received during the work; the user has sent only the initial instruction.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: pnpm/nx invocation issue (workaround above); json-server startup; zoneless/Material integration builds cleanly; booking persistence and guard design; seat geometry verified by unit tests (308 selectable elements, aisles, entrance, couch layout, state rules).\n   - Unverified: real browser behaviour (no browser available); visual layout; datepicker and snackbar runtime behaviour; the copy/behaviour of all AC items end-to-end. The snackbar exit animation may briefly show two toast DOM nodes (library behaviour).\n   - Build status: `pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run=false pnpm nx build cinescope --skip-nx-cache` succeeds with a bundle-size WARNING (≈600 kB vs 500 kB budget; 1 MB is the error threshold).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Only user message) \"Build the cinescope seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   - The latest message in the conversation is a system instruction requiring a text-only summary (no tool calls); it is not a user request to change scope.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Ticket 07 final pass: review every AC in spec section 10 against the code (especially data-testids in section 9, the datepicker/day-picker behaviour, redirects, toast texts, and the booking lifecycle), fix any gaps.\n   - Tick every box in spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md through 06-confirmation.md (including the non-AC boxes in 04, 06) and 07-final-pass.md, and update Status lines to done (only after verifying).\n   - Run the final `pnpm nx build cinescope` (with the env workaround) and confirm success; optionally run `pnpm nx lint cinescope` (not required).\n   - Re-run `pnpm nx test cinescope` after any changes.\n   - Check `.pnpm-store/` (untracked) — determine whether I created it and remove it only if confirmed to be a pnpm-created artefact (it was absent at the start, when git status was clean).\n   - Do not commit unless the user asks.\n   - Final report to the user: summarize what was built, the env workaround for pnpm verify-deps, that json-server must run on port 3000, that the browser UI could not be exercised (only build and unit tests verified), and the bundle-size warning.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I finished ticket work 01–06 in code and wrote unit specs. The most recent actions: created core/auditorium.spec.ts (rewritten cleanly), core/seat-units.spec.ts, checkout/checkout-validation.spec.ts, core/dates.spec.ts; fixed the seat-units.spec.ts ordering bug (removed `.reverse()`); ran `pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run=false pnpm nx test cinescope --skip-nx-cache`, which reported \"Test Files 5 passed (5)\" and \"Tests 26 passed (26)\". The previous successful build was run after the confirmation/routes change. Ticket checkboxes in spec/tickets are still unticked.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Directly in line with the user's request (\"implement the tickets in order; finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds\"): carry out the ticket 07 final pass — review the code against spec section 10 and section 9 (fix any mismatches), tick the boxes and Status lines in spec/tickets/01–07, re-run the build (`pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run=false pnpm nx build cinescope --skip-nx-cache`) and tests, check and clean up the untracked `.pnpm-store/` only if it was created by my work, then report to the user with the pnpm workaround and the untested-in-browser caveat. Do not commit.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/d875e994-7ce1-4d4f-b1bd-5d9c510e136a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d875e994-7ce1-4d4f-b1bd-5d9c510e136a","uuid":"7afd8263-3568-4a13-b3e8-908b709383f2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:05:42.519Z","isSynthetic":true}
